paperweight-chromebook (0.1.12-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add paperweight-expand-home: post-install script that migrates /home to an
    inserted SD card (partitions, formats ext4, rsyncs, writes /etc/fstab entry).
  * debian/control: add gdisk and rsync to Depends.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 14:51:27 -0500

paperweight-chromebook (0.1.11-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * debian/postinst: add GRUB_GFXPAYLOAD_LINUX=keep so the kernel
    framebuffer stays at the GRUB resolution for Plymouth.
  * debian/postrm: replace value-specific sed patterns with key-only
    patterns (/^GRUB_GFXMODE=/d, /^GRUB_GFXPAYLOAD_LINUX=/d) so removal
    works even if the user edited the values after install. Also remove
    GRUB_GFXPAYLOAD_LINUX on uninstall.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:02 +0000

paperweight-chromebook (0.1.10-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * debian/postinst: set GRUB_GFXMODE=1366x768,auto in /etc/default/grub
    so the GRUB theme renders at the Chromebook's native resolution.
    Runs update-grub on install. No-op if /etc/default/grub is absent.
  * debian/postrm: remove GRUB_GFXMODE=1366x768,auto on package removal.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:01 +0000

paperweight-chromebook (0.1.9-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * 20-keys.conf: bind F11 (F4 position) to fullscreen toggle, F5 (overview
    key) to layout toggle. Add $mod+top-row bindings that inject literal F1-F10
    into the focused window via wtype.
  * debian/control: add wtype to Depends.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

paperweight-chromebook (0.1.8-1) trixie; urgency=low

